+# Replication implementation review r6: response ledger
+
+Reviews: `docs/revision/roster/{sol,astra}-rep-impl-r6.md` (both reject; the five findings agree). Plan of record:
+`replication-plan.md` (unchanged). The new specific tests were run on commit 0711a21 before the fix: all 8 failed. Round
+5's items K1, K3 and K4 were incomplete; their completions are L1 to L5.
+
+| # | Correction (Sol #, Astra #) | Plan text | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| L1 | A comparison is a measurement only if it is well-formed as Run B writes it (boolean pass, list of problems, three numeric differences, not NaN; an infinite gain difference allowed); a missing or malformed comparison is an invalid record (rerun on resume, not continued in the analysis), never a mismatch; a fresh gate without a measured comparison exits 6 (invalid gate), not 4 (S1, A1) | s4: mismatch "round 1 differs from this run's doubling record"; "missing or nonfinite, keeps its validated frozen winner" | fixed in `rep_collect._gate_wellformed`, `_mismatch`, `run_queue`: test_a_malformed_comparison_is_an_invalid_record_not_a_mismatch (3 cases, analysis and resume; all failed first); test_a_gate_without_a_measured_comparison_does_not_pass_outside_smoke now expects exit 6 |
+| L2 | Every cell's continuation record is checked for a measured round-1 disagreement before any base-record exclusion, so an unscorable cell cannot hide a mismatch (S2, A2) | s4: a mismatch "stops all continuation, no continued winner of this run enters any result" | fixed in `rep_collect.collect`: test_a_measured_disagreement_stops_everything_even_when_the_cells_base_record_is_invalid (2 cases; both failed first) |
+| L3 | Queue construction treats a doubling record whose root is not an object as absent, and flags a cell only when `incomplete` is exactly true (S3, A3) | s4 | fixed in `rep_collect.flagged_cells`: test_queue_construction_treats_a_non_object_doubling_record_as_absent (failed first), test_queue_construction_survives_every_mutation_of_a_doubling_record |
+| L4 | The normalizer-after-division and finite-term checks are part of the shared validation: `cont_problem` (gate, continuation, resume, diagnostics selection) and `base_problem` (evaluation and the doubling's held-out result); the job must give N (S4, A4) | s4: "missing or invalid is unscorable" | fixed: test_a_saved_gate_or_continuation_with_a_normalizer_zero_after_division_is_rerun, test_a_doubling_record_with_a_normalizer_zero_after_division_makes_the_cell_unscorable (both failed first) |
+| L5 | The guard asserts one exact outcome per kind, in the analysis and on resume: a malformed continuation is not continued with the primary set kept and no mismatch, and is rerun; a malformed gate removes the primary set without a mismatch and is rerun; only a non-empty problems list is a mismatch (exit 4, no rerun); a well-formed provenance naming another job or run refuses the resume (plan section 5), a missing or malformed one is an invalid record. Completion claims of r5 corrected; ruling 10 amended (S5, A5) | s5: "reuse only this run's records" | test_every_mutation_of_every_record_kind_is_handled (7 kinds, collect and run_queue); done in `rep-impl-r5-response.md`, `rep-launcher-notes.md` |
+
+Checks: `uv run --frozen pytest -q docs/revision/followup3/` (173 pass). Launcher and harness unchanged (sha256 equal to
+the 47 of 47 log header). The round-3 smoke records re-collected: 72 of 72 scorable, 0 problems, audit counts for all
+18 R3 cells. All 76 Run B comparisons are well-formed; all 76 are identical, pass every round-1 check against their
+registered doubling and search records, and are not mismatches.
